==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*deyḱ-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*deikō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*déyḱti||to show, point out}} (reformed as a thematic verb). The perfect forms are derived from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*dḗyḱst}}.

Cognates include {{cog|osc|𐌃𐌄𐌝𐌊𐌖𐌌||to show, point out}}, {{cog|sa|दिशति|tr=diśáti}}, {{cog|grc|δείκνυμι}} and {{cog|ang|tǣċan}} (English {{m|ang|teach}}).

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|la|deicō}} {{qual|archaic}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|dīcō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-dico-long.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|irreg|dīcō}}

# I [[say]], [[utter]]; [[mention]]; [[talk]], [[speak]]
#: {{uxi|la|Salūtem '''dīcit'''.|lit=He '''says''' health.|He '''says''' hi.}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Genesis|1|3|quote='''dixit'''que Deus fiat lux et facta est lux|trans=And God '''said''': Be light made. And light was made.}}
#: {{syn|la|āiō|for|loquor}}
# I [[declare]], [[state]].
## I [[affirm]], [[assert]] (positively)
# I [[tell]]
#* '''c. 254–184 {{B.C.E.}}''', [[w:Plautus|Plautus]], [[w:Captivi|Captivi]] ("The Captives"), 623, ([https://web.archive.org/web/20130113120403/http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm English and Latin text])
#*: Eho '''dic''' mihi, quis illic igitur est?
#*:: Hey? '''Tell''' me, who is he then?
# I [[appoint]], [[name]], [[nominate]] (to an office)
# I [[call]], name
# {{lb|la|law|followed by {{m|la|ad}}}} I [[plead]] (before)
# I [[mean]], speak in [[reference]] to, [[refer]] to

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|irreg|dīcō}}
Old forms:
* paragogic infinitive present passive: {{m|la|dīcier}}
* singular imperative present active: {{m|la|dīce}} (= {{m|la|dīc}})
* gerundive: {{m|la|dīcundus}} (= {{m|la|dīcendus}})
* indicative future active: {{m|la|dicebo}}, {{m|la|dicebit}} <!-- length? -->

